Error: Jet.ValueThrownAway: This Int value is thrown away
  --> Tests/UI/discarded_pure_result.jet:6:29
    |
  6 | total: fn(a: Int, b: Int) { a + b }
    |                             ^^^^^
 Why: `total` has no return type, so it returns nothing and the value of its last line is lost
 Fix: If `total` should return it, write `-> Int` after its parameter list; to discard it on purpose, write `.drop("reason")`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.ValueThrownAway

Error: Jet.ValueThrownAway: The result of `double` is thrown away
  --> Tests/UI/discarded_pure_result.jet:9:5
    |
  9 |     double(3)
    |     ^^^^^^
 Why: `double` is pure (it has no effects and changes nothing through `&`), so this line does nothing
 Fix: Use the result, bind it with `result: double`, or write `.drop("reason")` if dropping it is intended
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.ValueThrownAway
